1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,783
So far the ruin has rooms, and places, and a voice.

2
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:08,291
Today it has things in it.

3
00:00:09,191 --> 00:00:12,670
There are sample canisters in the big room,

4
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:17,902
and a stone bowl at the back of the built one.

5
00:00:18,802 --> 00:00:23,585
A ship that flies up to either one takes it aboard.

6
00:00:25,385 --> 00:00:27,993
And when the bowl is taken,

7
00:00:28,443 --> 00:00:31,487
the game itself tells the story so.

8
00:00:32,687 --> 00:00:37,470
It takes three records to make a thing you can take.

9
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:41,413
The item says what the thing is.

10
00:00:41,863 --> 00:00:45,341
A place says where one of them lies.

11
00:00:45,791 --> 00:00:50,139
And a quest says what the story does about it.

12
00:00:51,939 --> 00:00:54,983
A quest can wait in two ways.

13
00:00:55,883 --> 00:01:00,665
It can wait for a kind of thing, by its key,

14
00:01:01,115 --> 00:01:03,289
and that's for ordinary finds.

15
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:07,233
Or it can wait for a word,

16
00:01:07,683 --> 00:01:12,465
and that's for the one thing the whole ruin is about.

17
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:16,409
The game sends that word by itself.

18
00:01:17,609 --> 00:01:21,087
Items live in a section of their own.

19
00:01:21,987 --> 00:01:24,596
I find the comment above Characters,

20
00:01:25,046 --> 00:01:28,524
and I type the new section above it.

21
00:01:29,424 --> 00:01:33,772
Two hashes for the section, and three for the item.

22
00:01:35,572 --> 00:01:37,311
The key is canister,

23
00:01:37,761 --> 00:01:41,239
and that's the word everything else will use.

24
00:01:42,139 --> 00:01:44,313
Type says item, slash, quest,

25
00:01:44,763 --> 00:01:47,372
which means the story carries it.

26
00:01:48,272 --> 00:01:51,315
And Art is what it looks like.

27
00:01:53,115 --> 00:01:56,593
That last line matters more than you'd think.

28
00:01:57,493 --> 00:02:01,407
A ship takes a thing by flying into it,

29
00:02:01,857 --> 00:02:05,335
and only some shapes can be flown into.

30
00:02:06,235 --> 00:02:09,278
The table on the page lists them.

31
00:02:10,178 --> 00:02:13,222
Leave the line out, or misspell it,

32
00:02:13,672 --> 00:02:18,020
and the thing just sits there for the whole game.

33
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,659
Lint won't tell you.

34
00:02:21,859 --> 00:02:24,033
Now a place for it.

35
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:29,280
This is a place like the ones from Lecture three,

36
00:02:29,730 --> 00:02:31,470
with two new lines.

37
00:02:32,370 --> 00:02:37,152
Item, and the item's key, means one of these lies here.

38
00:02:38,052 --> 00:02:41,096
And Qty, three, means it's worth three.

39
00:02:42,896 --> 00:02:46,374
The crew takes all three in one go.

40
00:02:47,274 --> 00:02:50,752
So this is one thing to pick up,

41
00:02:51,202 --> 00:02:54,246
and it's worth three in the hold.

42
00:02:54,696 --> 00:02:57,304
Remember that for the next step.

43
00:02:58,504 --> 00:03:01,548
Here's the quest that waits for them.

44
00:03:02,448 --> 00:03:06,796
Everything in it is from Class one, except one line.

45
00:03:07,696 --> 00:03:09,435
Done when, collect, canister.

46
00:03:09,885 --> 00:03:13,363
The word after collect is the item's key.

47
00:03:15,163 --> 00:03:16,902
And here's the catch.

48
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:19,541
The game counts pick-ups,

49
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:23,470
it doesn't count what a pick-up is worth.

50
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,543
My cache is one pick-up.

51
00:03:27,443 --> 00:03:30,052
If I write collect three canister,

52
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:33,546
the game waits for three separate pick-ups,

53
00:03:33,996 --> 00:03:37,039
and with one cache, it waits forever.

54
00:03:38,839 --> 00:03:41,013
Lint says clean either way.

55
00:03:41,463 --> 00:03:44,941
So I write collect canister, with no number.

56
00:03:46,741 --> 00:03:51,089
The description gets a second paragraph, after a blank line.

57
00:03:51,989 --> 00:03:54,598
The first says what to do,

58
00:03:55,048 --> 00:03:57,222
the second says what's known.

59
00:03:58,422 --> 00:04:01,465
Now the thing the ruin was hiding.

60
00:04:02,365 --> 00:04:04,974
First the item, a stone bowl.

61
00:04:05,874 --> 00:04:11,091
Then I go back to the Niche, and I change two lines.

62
00:04:12,891 --> 00:04:18,109
On the Roles line I add a comma, and relic underscore piece.

63
00:04:19,009 --> 00:04:20,748
That role isn't mine.

64
00:04:21,198 --> 00:04:23,372
It's the game's own word,

65
00:04:23,822 --> 00:04:26,865
the way entrance was in Lecture three.

66
00:04:27,765 --> 00:04:32,113
It means the thing in this place is the piece.

67
00:04:33,913 --> 00:04:36,087
And then Item, stone bowl.

68
00:04:36,987 --> 00:04:38,726
It takes both lines.

69
00:04:39,176 --> 00:04:42,220
The role alone is an empty place,

70
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:46,148
and the item alone is just another find.

71
00:04:47,348 --> 00:04:49,087
And the second quest.

72
00:04:49,987 --> 00:04:52,161
Done when, signal, hollow taken.

73
00:04:53,961 --> 00:04:57,439
Now, nothing in my file sends that word,

74
00:04:57,889 --> 00:05:00,063
and lint still says clean.

75
00:05:00,963 --> 00:05:03,572
That's because the game sends it.

76
00:05:04,472 --> 00:05:08,820
It takes the key of the ruin, which is hollow,

77
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:11,443
and it adds underscore taken.

78
00:05:13,243 --> 00:05:14,983
It's the ruin's key.

79
00:05:15,433 --> 00:05:19,346
It's not the place's, and it's not the thing's.

80
00:05:20,246 --> 00:05:24,593
Lint will catch you if you use either of those.

81
00:05:26,393 --> 00:05:28,567
The word is sent once.

82
00:05:29,467 --> 00:05:35,120
So the quest has to be running before anybody can reach the bowl.

83
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:38,613
That's why this one starts at once.

84
00:05:39,813 --> 00:05:42,422
I run lint, and it's clean.

85
00:05:43,322 --> 00:05:46,365
Now I take out the Art line,

86
00:05:46,815 --> 00:05:48,989
and lint is still clean.

87
00:05:49,889 --> 00:05:55,107
That's the one to check by eye, so I put it back.

88
00:05:56,907 --> 00:05:59,080
Then I start the game.

89
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:02,589
Both quests are in the list.

90
00:06:03,489 --> 00:06:07,837
I fly into the Nave and straight at the canisters.

91
00:06:08,287 --> 00:06:13,070
There's the pick-up, times three, and the first quest is done.

92
00:06:14,870 --> 00:06:18,783
Now the Gallery, all the way to the back.

93
00:06:19,683 --> 00:06:21,857
And there's the stone bowl.

94
00:06:22,307 --> 00:06:26,220
I take it, and the second quest is done.

95
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:31,033
And I never wrote the line that said so.

96
00:06:32,233 --> 00:06:33,972
Now it's your turn.

97
00:06:34,872 --> 00:06:39,220
Add a second cache, and make the quest want both.

98
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:44,467
Make the canisters appear only when the ship comes near.

99
00:06:45,367 --> 00:06:50,150
Make the bowl appear only when Comms has heard Rook out.

100
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:55,863
Then break one line where lint can see it,

101
00:06:56,313 --> 00:06:58,487
and one where it can't.

102
00:06:59,387 --> 00:07:05,039
Later in this class, someone goes in and takes that bowl by hand.
